This code aims to estimate depression severity (PHQ-8 score) using both a tree-based machine learning model and a deep learning algorithm. The analysis explores the most informative features using filter-based feature selection and evaluates prediction performance across different demographic groups (gender, race/ethnicity, and their intersection).

🔧 Project Overview
Objective: Predict the PHQ-8 depression scores for each participant.

ML Algorithms Used:

✅ Tree-Based Model: Random Forest Regressor

✅ Deep Learning Model: Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP)

Feature Selection: Filter method using Mutual Information Regression (MIR)

Performance Metrics:

📈 Pearson’s Correlation (r)

📉 Absolute Relative Error (RE)

📁 Dataset
Participant features include demographic, behavioral, and psychological attributes.

Target variable: PHQ-8 score

Demographics considered:

Gender: Male, Female

Race/Ethnicity: African American, White American, Hispanic

Intersectional Groups (e.g., African American Female, White American Male, etc.)

🔍 Methodology
Preprocessing:

Data cleaned and standardized

Categorical features encoded

Missing values imputed

Feature Selection:

Used Mutual Information Regression to rank features by relevance to PHQ-8 score

Experimented with different values of k (e.g., 5, 10, 20, 30)

Modeling:

Trained Random Forest and MLP on selected features

Performed stratified evaluation across:

All participants

Gender groups

Race/ethnicity groups

Gender × Race/Ethnicity combinations

Evaluation:

Reported Pearson’s r and Absolute Relative Error (RE)

